  {
    "id": "wil",
    "name": "Wil Nettle",
    "role": "Shepherd",
    "look": {
      "g": "m",
      "skin": 1,
      "hair": "#a89a80",
      "cloth": "#6a6a4a",
      "accent": "#d8c890",
      "hat": "hood"
    },
    "greeting": [
      "Mind the pen. The ewes bite."
    ],
    "talk": [
      {
        "label": "What do you keep?",
        "lines": [
          "Forty ewes, a ram, and a dog who thinks the ram is his. The Downs grass is good. The boars are not."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Seen anything odd?",
        "lines": [
          "The bats come out of the Delve at dusk, in a cloud. They used to come back before dawn. Now they stay out."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "services": []
  },
  {
    "id": "corley",
    "name": "Corley Reeve",
    "role": "Miner, second shift",
    "look": {
      "g": "m",
      "skin": 0,
      "hair": "#7a6a5a",
      "cloth": "#4a4a4a",
      "accent": "#c8a050",
      "hat": "helm"
    },
    "greeting": [
      "I am not leaving. Not until my crew is out of there."
    ],
    "talk": [
      {
        "label": "Why are you here?",
        "lines": [
          "I was on the second shift. I came up for a break and the water came down the main shaft behind me. I have sat at this door every day since."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "What is down there?",
        "lines": [
          "Rats, bats, wretches that were my friends, boars that came in through the broken wall. And at the bottom, the Foreman. The old foreman. Edda Marrow's brother. He still gives orders. He does not give them to people."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "services": [
      {
        "kind": "quests"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "guide",
    "name": "Reeve Isolde Penn",
    "role": "Guide to newcomers",
    "look": {
      "g": "f",
      "skin": 2,
      "hair": "#7a4a2a",
      "cloth": "#3f6a58",
      "accent": "#e0c060",
      "hat": "none"
    },
    "greeting": [
      "You are the one who came up the south road. I am Isolde Penn. I keep newcomers out of the Sump and out of trouble.",
      "Ask me whatever you like. Everyone does, the first morning."
    ],
    "talk": [
      {
        "label": "How do I get around?",
        "lines": [
          "Click the ground to walk. Scroll or press plus and minus to zoom, and M shows the whole map.",
          "Click a person to talk to them, or a tree, rock or pond to work it. Hold the mouse over anything and a small card tells you what it is."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "How does fighting work?",
        "lines": [
          "Click a monster to start a fight. It plays out in turns on a grid. Move on the blue tiles, pick an ability from the bar, then click your target.",
          "Your weapon sets your reach. Blades and daggers fight up close, a bow reaches six tiles and a staff five. If it goes badly you can flee, though the monsters stay angry for a moment."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "What is hit chance?",
        "lines": [
          "A weapon swing lands about three times in four against a foe your own level. A higher skill or accuracy gear improves it, and a tougher foe lowers it. It never falls below one in twenty.",
          "Spells never miss, unless something has blinded you. Open your stats with C to see your own number."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Skills, gear and bag",
        "lines": [
          "K opens your skills, where you spend a point each time you level. I is your bag, E is what you wear, and C shows your stats.",
          "Better gear comes from drops, from the smith, and from the shops. Rare and legendary pieces carry powers of their own."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Gathering and crafting",
        "lines": [
          "Chop trees, mine rock, fish the pond and snare rabbits. Pine is level one, birch ten, oak twenty and willow thirty. Dark-green narrow trees are pines, pale trunks are birch.",
          "Take what you gather to the smith and the cook. They turn it into gear and food."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Portals, checkpoints and signing out",
        "lines": [
          "Press T to cast the town portal. It takes a few breaths, you have to stand still, and it will not work in a fight. It carries you to your last checkpoint.",
          "Walk into a safe place near a bellstone or a town gate and it becomes your checkpoint. That is where you wake after a fall or a sign-out.",
          "One warning. Sign out in the middle of a fight inside a dungeon and you lose what that delve gave you."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Where should I start?",
        "lines": [
          "Warden Osbric stands by the Crown Tower, north of here. He wants a stranger with fresh eyes. His first errand is easy.",
          "Tam at the stable has moss imps chewing his harness, south of the gate. Clear three and you will have earned a hearing."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "services": []
  },
  {
    "id": "tansy",
    "name": "Tansy Gale",
    "role": "Landlady, the Salt Lantern",
    "look": {
      "g": "f",
      "skin": 1,
      "hair": "#b8b0a0",
      "cloth": "#4a5a6a",
      "accent": "#e8d8a0",
      "hat": "none"
    },
    "greeting": [
      "Mind the rope on the floor. The fog gets in everywhere and brings the damp with it.",
      "Beds are eight bits. The fish is good. Ask nothing about the cellar."
    ],
    "talk": [
      {
        "label": "What is Innsharrow like?",
        "lines": [
          "Fog, rope and tar. We are a fishing town. That is the story and we all keep to it.",
          "The old families come in on the first of the month, drink one cup each, and leave before the tide turns. I pour. I do not listen."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "The harbor bells",
        "lines": [
          "They ring when a certain kind of boat comes in. No, I will not say which kind."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "services": [
      {
        "kind": "inn",
        "cost": 8
      },
      {
        "kind": "shop",
        "shop": "salt_lantern"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "maid",
    "name": "Aelwyn",
    "role": "Tavern hand",
    "look": {
      "g": "f",
      "skin": 2,
      "hair": "#3a2a22",
      "cloth": "#6a5a4a",
      "accent": "#c8a860",
      "hat": "none"
    },
    "greeting": [
      "If you are here to tell me who I am, do not. I have heard it. Twice today.",
      "I am carrying plates. Plates do not ask questions."
    ],
    "talk": [
      {
        "label": "You look like someone I have seen.",
        "lines": [
          "Everyone says that. It is the nose. Please stop looking at my nose."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Do you want to leave?",
        "lines": [
          "I want to hit something. A lot. The boars in the dunes would do. They do not look at my face."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "services": [
      {
        "kind": "quests"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "jory",
    "name": "Harbormaster Jory Fenn",
    "role": "Harbormaster",
    "look": {
      "g": "m",
      "skin": 1,
      "hair": "#5a5a5a",
      "cloth": "#2a4a6a",
      "accent": "#d8c060",
      "hat": "hood"
    },
    "greeting": [
      "Every boat that ties up here, I know. Every boat that does not, I also know. Fishing licence is free. Honesty is extra."
    ],
    "talk": [
      {
        "label": "How is the harbor?",
        "lines": [
          "Busy for a fishing port. We land a lot of cargo for a place that lands so few fish. I keep my ledger tidy and my eyes on the ledger."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "Where do I fish?",
        "lines": [
          "Piers out to the south. Trout near the shore, level ten. Salmon farther out, level twenty. Tuna at the pier heads, thirty. You will want a better rod each time. Wick sells them."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "services": [
      {
        "kind": "quests"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "wick",
    "name": "Wick Marlowe",
    "role": "Net-loft keeper",
    "look": {
      "g": "m",
      "skin": 2,
      "hair": "#6a3a22",
      "cloth": "#6a5a3a",
      "accent": "#a8c8d8",
      "hat": "none"
    },
    "greeting": [
      "Nets, rods, hooks, bait. If it can be caught I sell something that catches it."
    ],
    "talk": [
      {
        "label": "Which rod?",
        "lines": [
          "Ash for trout. Oak for salmon. For tuna you want a lantern rod, and I cannot sell you one. The only ones I have seen came out of the water on their own."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "services": [
      {
        "kind": "shop",
        "shop": "harbor_tackle"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "brisket",
    "name": "Brisket Hale",
    "role": "Cook at the Cookhouse",
    "look": {
      "g": "m",
      "skin": 1,
      "hair": "#8a6a4a",
      "cloth": "#d8d0c0",
      "accent": "#e0a040",
      "hat": "none"
    },
    "greeting": [
      "Use the range. Cook your own, or buy mine. Raw fish makes poor friends."
    ],
    "talk": [
      {
        "label": "What should I cook?",
        "lines": [
          "Trout at ten. Salmon at twenty. Tuna at thirty, and take it off the heat early or it turns to rope. A cooked fish heals more than any bread."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "services": [
      {
        "kind": "shop",
        "shop": "cookhouse"
      },
      {
        "kind": "quests"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "orla",
    "name": "Dame Orla Quill",
    "role": "Master of the archery yard",
    "look": {
      "g": "f",
      "skin": 1,
      "hair": "#c8c0b0",
      "cloth": "#4a6a4a",
      "accent": "#d8b060",
      "hat": "none"
    },
    "greeting": [
      "Draw to the ear. Loose on the breath. Anyone who tells you different has not hit anything."
    ],
    "talk": [
      {
        "label": "Teach me.",
        "lines": [
          "A bow reaches six tiles, so you fight with space. Stay at the edge of their reach and keep moving. Anything that closes on you, you have already lost the exchange.",
          "Buy a birch bow before you buy anything else. Then go and shoot gnashers on the road until you stop flinching."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "services": [
      {
        "kind": "shop",
        "shop": "archery_yard"
      },
      {
        "kind": "quests"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "sable",
    "name": "Sable Quist",
    "role": "Regular at the Gull's Rest",
    "look": {
      "g": "f",
      "skin": 2,
      "hair": "#1a1a1a",
      "cloth": "#3a3a4a",
      "accent": "#a090c0",
      "hat": "hood"
    },
    "greeting": [
      "You are not from the families. Good. That means you will listen to me and then forget me."
    ],
    "talk": [
      {
        "label": "What do the families do?",
        "lines": [
          "They land things at night. Crates with no marks. Men who do not give names. Sometimes they ask the harbor bells to ring twice and the tide to go out early."
        ]
      },
      {
        "label": "The Pale Circle",
        "lines": [
          "I never said that word. I said a man in a white mask paid for my silence. I took it. Whoever asks next gets the same story."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "services": []
  },
  {
    "id": "osgar",
    "name": "Osgar Thorne",
    "role": "Trapper",
    "look": {
      "g": "m",
      "skin": 2,
      "hair": "#3a2a22",
      "cloth": "#4a5a3a",
      "accent": "#c0a050",
      "hat": "hood"
    },
    "greeting": [
      "Snares, nets, pits. If it walks, I can make it stop."
    ],
    "talk": [
      {
        "label": "What traps work?",
        "lines": [
          "Rope snares for small game. Net traps for wolves, and they are not enough. Pit traps hold anything that is not clever. The pack-lord is clever."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "services": [
      {
        "kind": "shop",
        "shop": "trappers_stall"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "warden_leofric",
    "name": "Warden Leofric",
    "role": "Warden of Wargwatch",
    "look": {
      "g": "m",
      "skin": 1,
      "hair": "#7a7a7a",
      "cloth": "#3a4a3a",
      "accent": "#b8c0a0",
      "hat": "hood"
    },
    "greeting": [
      "You have the look of someone who finishes things. Good. I have a pack that needs finishing."
    ],
    "talk": [
      {
        "label": "What is wrong with the wolves?",
        "lines": [
          "Someone is feeding them meat that has been in the ground. It does not rot. It makes them hungry, and then it makes them worse.",
          "The trail runs to the Nameless Cairns. I have not gone in. I am not proud of that."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "services": [
      {
        "kind": "quests"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "bowyer_ansel",
    "name": "Ansel Brack",
    "role": "Bowyer",
    "look": {
      "g": "m",
      "skin": 2,
      "hair": "#5a3a22",
      "cloth": "#8a6a3a",
      "accent": "#6a8a5a",
      "hat": "none"
    },
    "greeting": [
      "Oak for the road, willow for the long shot. Ask me about draw weights and I will not stop."
    ],
    "talk": [
      {
        "label": "Which bow?",
        "lines": [
          "Oak for most. Willow if you have the coin and the shoulders. Either way, do not shoot a wight. Fire and blunt, as the saying goes."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "services": [
      {
        "kind": "shop",
        "shop": "bowyer"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "smoker_edda",
    "name": "Edda Fell",
    "role": "Smokehouse keeper",
    "look": {
      "g": "f",
      "skin": 1,
      "hair": "#4a3a32",
      "cloth": "#8a5a3a",
      "accent": "#d8a860",
      "hat": "none"
    },
    "greeting": [
      "Venison, smoked slow. Do not ask what kind of wood. The wood is none of your business."
    ],
    "talk": [
      {
        "label": "Any news?",
        "lines": [
          "The Warden has been quiet for a week. When the Warden is quiet, someone is about to be sent somewhere."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "services": [
      {
        "kind": "shop",
        "shop": "smokehouse"
      }
    ]
  }
]
